  "id": "acidtest",
  "neon": "#e8c34a",
  "note": "THE ACID TEST — an assay counter on Kiln Lane for people back in off the flats with something\nheavy in a bag.\n\nThe tile's prose: a small frontage, a heavy door, a brass plate reading THE ACID TEST, WEIGHED AND\nSTATED, NO OPINIONS OFFERED, and a queue outside some mornings. The window is a slot above head\nheight with a bar across it: nobody inside can see the street and nobody outside can see in.\n\nSo the front is mostly wall: precast piers at the corners, the heavy door in a steel surround under\na hood, the barred slot high up, the name on the fascia and the brass plate by the door. A rail of\nbollards marks where the queue stands. A lamp over the door is the only light, because it opens\nearly.\n\nThe walls are board-formed concrete. They were `ty_precast`, which is in the window-grid family\nand painted a row of windows onto a building whose point is that you can't see in.",
  "pal": "ty_quay_deck",
